<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Phase 4 Best in Slot Gear list for Frost Mage DPS in Wrath of the Lich King Classic. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from Icecrown Citadel. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">Best in Slot Gear for Frost Mage DPS Phase 4</h2>This phase we get the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item-set=883/bloodmages-regalia">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Bloodmage's Regalia</span></a> and this brings with it a new system for tier sets, we have to buy the lowest item level version of it using <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49426/emblem-of-frost">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_frostemblem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Frost</span></a>. We then use these base items with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=52025/vanquishers-mark-of-sanctification">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_shieldofthetemplar.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vanquisher's Mark of Sanctification</span></a> and then <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=52028/vanquishers-mark-of-sanctification">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_judgementsofthejust.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vanquisher's Mark of Sanctification</span></a> to upgrade them to item level 264 and 277 respectively. These are very well optimized items that are as good or better than same ilvl items of the same slot, regardless of the actual set bonuses which previously always felt like they were accounted for when itemizing the tier gear.<br/>
<br/>Frost Mage isn't very strong for PVE, since it's mostly a PVP focused specialization, if you want to min-max it and try and make it work this will be the set you'll be aiming for.<br/>
